T1, T3 and M3 C3S with various types and amounts of foreign ions were systematically synthesized (see Table 5
). Special attention is given to the amount of both Al2O3 and Fe2O3, which are amphoteric in nature and are usually considered top provide the best evidence to assess the effect of foreign ions on the IR spectra of C3S. Fig. 5
 shows the IR spectra of T1, T3 and M3 C3S. The IR spectra of the C3S samples with different compositions but the same polymorphic form are almost identical. There are no changes in the peak position or number of peaks in the IR spectra of T1 C3S with single doping of either Al2O3 or Fe2O3 (see Fig. 5a). The IR spectra of T3 C3S with single doping of Al2O3 or Fe2O3 and with combined doping of multiple ions are shown in Fig. 5b. No changes are observed in the IR spectra of T3 C3S with different compositions. Similarly, no effect of Al3+ on the IR spectra of M3 C3S is observed (see Fig. 5c). However, Fe3+ has been shown to have a slight effect on the IR spectrum of M3 C3S. With increasing amount of Fe3+, slight shifts of the symmetric stretching bands (ν3) to lower waver number are observed for M3 C3S (Fig. 5c). However, the most intense peak is still centred at lower wave numbers of approximately 924–932cm−1, as described above. Thus, changes in the IR spectra of C3S solid solutions mainly result from changes in the polymorphic structures. The introduction of substituent ions has a weak effect on the IR spectra of C3S. Consequently, IR spectroscopy can be used to identify the polymorphs of C3S.
